@call c01 chest_pain start=14:02:10
@patient age=62 sex=male weight_kg=95 complaint="chest pressure radiating to left arm" allergies=NKDA home_meds="lisinopril, atorvastatin" history="hypertension, high cholesterol"
@traps STEMI
RD: Medic 14, respond priority one, sixty-two year old male, chest pain.  >> dispatch:chest pain "chest pain"
GAP 3
M1: Medic 14 on scene.  >> time:eTimes.06 "on scene"
GAP 4
M1: Sir, I'm Dana with the ambulance. What's going on today?
PT: It's like an elephant on my chest. Started about forty minutes ago, goes down my left arm.
M1: Any allergies to medications?
PT: No, none.
M1: What do you take at home?
PT: Lisinopril and, uh, atorvastatin.
TAP knock +label
M2: First set, BP 158 over 94, pulse 104, sat 95 on room air.  >> vital:bp=158/94 "BP 158 over 94"; vital:hr=104 "pulse 104"; vital:spo2=95 "sat 95"
GAP 3
M1: Let's get a 12 lead on him.  >> proc:12-lead ECG "12 lead"
GAP 8
TAP button +label
M1: Giving 324 of aspirin, chewed.  >> med:aspirin,324,,PO "324 of aspirin, chewed"
GAP 5
M2: Twelve lead shows elevation in two, three and aVF. Looks like a STEMI, I'm transmitting.
GAP 4
TAP snap +label
M1: Nitro 0.4 sublingual, his pressure can take it.  >> med:nitroglycerin,0.4,,SL "Nitro 0.4 sublingual"
GAP 12
TAP button -
GAP 12
M2: Got an 18 in the left AC.  >> proc:IV access "18 in the left AC"
GAP 4
M2: Repeat, 142 over 88, heart rate 98, pain's down to a 6 out of 10.  >> vital:bp=142/88 "142 over 88"; vital:hr=98 "heart rate 98"; vital:pain=6 "6 out of 10"
GAP 3
M1: We're transporting to Mercy, cath lab activated.  >> time:eTimes.09 "We're transporting"
GAP 6
TAP knock +label
M1: Second nitro, 0.4 under the tongue.  >> med:nitroglycerin,0.4,,SL "Second nitro, 0.4 under the tongue"
GAP 10
M1: Arrived at Mercy.  >> time:eTimes.11 "Arrived at Mercy"
GAP 14
TAP button +label
M1: Giving report to the charge nurse now, transfer of care.  >> time:eTimes.12 "transfer of care"
KNOCK3
